2.bug_scenario:
When rendering C++ source with Highlight.js (using highlight rather than highlightAuto), lines like:

    Eigen::VectorXd vector(5);
    vector<<1,2,3,4,5;

are mis-highlighted (or not highlighted at all) beyond the “<<” operator.  The highlighter’s C++ grammar treats the “<<” as a left-shift operator (or as an opening angle bracket for templates) but then fails to re-enter an expression context that would consume the initializer list.  As a result, everything after that point is rendered as plain text instead of C++ code.
